        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "556884c7-c72a-5836-a672-0e3ec744482f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jeffrey Jey, Maurizio Lobina, Gabry Ponte\n- Organizations: Eiffel 65\n- Products: \"Blue (Da Ba Dee)\", \"Move Your Body\", \"Europop\", \"Un'altra Come Te\"\n- Topics: release history, notable works, remix/reference\n\nFacts:\n- Eiffel 65 is an Italian musical group consisting of Jeffrey Jey, Maurizio Lobina, and Gabry Ponte.\n- On 15 January 1999, Eiffel 65 released \"Blue (Da Ba Dee)\" as the lead single from their debut album \"Europop\".\n- \"Blue (Da Ba Dee)\" is a song by Eiffel 65.\n- In 1999, Eiffel 65 became known mainly for the high-charting singles \"Blue (Da Ba Dee)\" and \"Move Your Body\" and for the studio album \"Europop\".\n- Club Test 01 mentions a re-imagined version of Eiffel 65's previous hit \"Blue (Da Ba Dee)\", followed by an English version and remix of \"Un'altra Come Te\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
